From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/105] PC5: Direct3D 9 textures keep their size where
 Microsoft's are read (Wine patch 0907)

Resident Evil 3's Seamless HD mod reads a texture's width and the address
of its locked pixels straight from the object, at the offsets Microsoft's
d3d9.dll has: Wine's layout gave it other fields, so it skipped every HD
picture. Wine's own d3d9 now keeps them there on 32-bit.
---
